WEBVTT

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:05.950
The Gadgets and combat cyborgs launched an attack on Surface HQ.

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:10.580
The attack was brilliantly executed, paralyzing HQ within minutes.

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.160
It was as if they knew everything about the facility and its defenses.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:19.990
During the battle with the combat cyborgs,
Ginga was kidnapped, and Subaru was badly wounded.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:24.880
And with its forces deployed,
the defenseless Riot Force 6 HQ was destroyed,

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.500
with the remaining members left gravely wounded.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:32.420
Erio and Caro were shot down, and Vivio was kidnapped.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:37.020
It’s the worst possible situation. What’s going to happen to us?

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.000
And what about Subaru?

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:05.960
The things that I can do for you and no one else

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:11.660
I honestly feel and wish for those

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:18.380
I am frozen by uncertainties

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:24.620
By the rules I have been relying on

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:30.320
My past embellished with excuses

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.520
I want to get over it

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.800
Staining the stars in heaven scarlet

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:41.270
Gather the grains of miracles

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:44.530
Before the still, unseen night

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:47.810
I want to tell you that I am escaping from illusions

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:50.990
The twilight moon calls out to me

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:54.080
Removing my veil of delusions

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:57.290
My hidden, deceitful self

00:01:57.290 --> 00:02:01.170
And took all of my weaknesses

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:07.630
I don’t want words that seem passionate

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:17.050
The fact that I’m here right now is my truth

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:32.460
We’re on the scene above
the Time-Space Administrative Bureau’s

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:35.960
Midchilda Surface HQ,
which was attacked by terrorists yesterday.

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.680
There’s been no announcement from
the Bureau regarding the details of the incident,

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.100
the damage to the facility, or the number of casualties.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:49.430
There seems to have been a message from
the responsible group immediately after the incident,

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:55.920
but the Public Relations Department has said that it’ll only release it after detailed analysis.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:57.890
Why?

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:59.770
Why in the ever-loving hell is this happening?

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:01.660
Have you been able to contact that son of a bitch?

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:04.240
The line’s been changed,

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.240
and the research facility is empty.

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:14.410
We’ve given him more than enough funding up until now, so why?

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:16.410
Where the hell did Auris get to!?

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:18.750
She’s working on a counterplan.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.180
She’s discussing matters with the security division and the other parties involved.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:29.260
Lt. Colonel Yagami, a pleasure to see you.

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:33.230
Major Auris, may I speak to you for a moment later on?

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.800
There’s something I want to ask you.

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:39.560
I have a conference now. I’ll contact you when I’m free.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:40.340
Very well.

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:02.930
It’s a mess.

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:07.100
Lt. Signum, how were things at the hospital?

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:10.760
All the wounded members have made it through the worst.

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:12.090
Is that so?

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:13.470
I’m glad.

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:14.970
Where’s Captain Takamachi?

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:15.940
Inside.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.850
How is she?

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:19.560
The same as always.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.380
She’s performing her work well.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:23.760
Once she’d confirmed that Vivio was kidnapped

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:28.360
and that the wounded members were taken care of,
she hasn’t even taken a break.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:29.490
Really?

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.770
I’ll take care of this.

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:35.070
You get to the hospital too.

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:36.670
B-But...

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:38.740
Go see her.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:39.900
Yes, ma’am.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.820
Nanoha, it’s Teana.

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:47.090
Ah. What is it?

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:50.850
Lt. Signum has taken over for me.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:53.280
I’m going to the hospital for a while.

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:54.020
Okay.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:57.480
Captain Fate should be heading there as well.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:58.660
All right.

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:03.390
Um... may I tell Subaru and Shari what you told me earlier?

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:04.770
Sure.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:07.900
If you think it’ll cheer them up, tell them.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:09.330
I’ll leave the choice to you.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:11.610
Understood. I’ll be back later.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:13.290
Okay. Take care.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.820
I’m sorry. I’m so sorry.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:41.040
I was in charge while you were gone, and I still couldn’t protect them.

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:45.230
It’s not your fault, Shari.

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:46.110
Don’t cry.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:52.560
About Vivio, how am I going to apologize to Nanoha and everyone?

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:58.330
Don’t force yourself.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:01.000
You were hurt really badly.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.040
I’m fine.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:05.070
Compared to Zafira, my wounds were light.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:09.680
Zafira shielded me from the worst of it.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.450
Me too.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:15.080
Rein protected me.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:18.980
If I hadn’t been in Unison with Rein, I’d be worm food now.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:21.730
I heard from Marie.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:24.000
Rein will wake up tonight.

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:30.350
But Zafira will take a while to fully recover.

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:31.950
And Vice...

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:36.370
Even if he’s through the worst, for a long time he’ll...

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:50.340
Tia.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.510
I brought you some snacks.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:57.180
None of you have really eaten, right?

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:00.100
Thank you so much.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:03.590
Thanks, Tia.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:11.360
You can move your arm now...

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:16.860
The nerve cables got fried, so I can’t move it well yet.

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:19.330
They say it’ll be back to normal in a few days.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.780
I see.

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:22.790
How much have you told the kids?

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:26.710
About how Ginny and I were born, stuff like that...

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:29.040
Sorry to keep it from you.

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:34.140
I’m the one who told Subaru not to tell you, that she should keep the truth about her body a secret for a while.

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:35.990
Not at all.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:40.520
Erio.

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.900
Oh. Right.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:46.350
Subaru, do you want some hot soup?

00:07:46.350 --> 00:07:48.340
They’re selling it at the cafeteria. I’ll get some.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:52.740
We’ll be back.

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:02.620
Tia, I’m sorry.

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:06.120
What are you sorry for?

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:10.090
For running ahead instead of listening to Nanoha and me?

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:13.550
Or that you got yourself
badly hurt and made everyone worry?

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:14.320
All of it.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:18.300
You better apologize to Mach Caliber too later.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:20.270
She’s in pretty bad shape.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:21.620
Yeah...

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:24.440
Hey, Ginga’s still alive, right?

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:29.390
I think she can come back from that level of damage.

00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:33.360
They were talking about recovering the Type-0s, so I don’t think they’ll...

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.060
...kill her, right?

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:37.760
Then you’ve got a chance to save her.

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:41.820
Nanoha was saying that she thinks that after this,

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:47.450
we’ll be changing our mission from
looking for the Relics to chasing after Scaglietti.

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:51.300
What happened to Ginga bothers me too.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:55.700
But if Riot Force 6 is going to act, then we can save her as a team.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:59.500
Erio, Caro, the captains,
and the Long Arch are upset too

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:06.400
that they lost what was important
to them and that they couldn’t protect it.

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:10.360
So, this time we won’t fail them.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:14.320
We’ll protect them and take back what was stolen.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:15.640
We’ll save her.

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:16.740
We’ll save <i>everyone.</i>

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:25.320
So what did you want to ask me?

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:28.040
About Lt. General Regius Gaiz’s work.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:31.030
A large portion of that information is classified.

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:34.550
There’s very little I can tell you as an individual.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:37.320
Can I just ask?

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:41.430
Well, where I should begin?

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:45.600
Start with the Combat Cyborg Incident
that you were in charge of, Major.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:50.720
Including Ginga and Subaru if you can, and their mom.

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:55.520
The basic idea behind the combat cyborgs was to produce a humanoid combat machine.

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:58.490
This research has been around for a long time.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:01.440
And by a long time,
I mean since the old calendar was in use.

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:04.260
A mechanical weapon created in the form of a human.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:08.870
The idea’s been developed
on many worlds and in many forms,

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:12.040
but there aren’t many examples of it actually working.

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:15.330
Then, the research underwent a dramatic evolution.

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:17.800
It was only 25 years ago.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:22.750
The combination of machinery
and biotechnology is nothing special.

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:27.010
Artificial organs and bones
have been around for a long time.

00:10:27.010 --> 00:10:27.770
But...

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:33.010
The function of those is to compensate for lost ability,
which is very different from strengthening that ability.

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:37.530
There are also problems with rejection and maintenance during long use.

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:40.060
But the combat cyborgs were different, you see.

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:44.910
Those bastards got around that problem by
screwing around with the genetic code of their subjects.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:50.070
During birth, they would become the base for the combat cyborgs.

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:55.460
They are children, but modified
able to accept mechanical body parts.

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:59.430
<i>He</i> created technology to allow that to happen.

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:02.850
That would be Jail Scaglietti.

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:08.750
Eleven years ago, back before I knew that the man named Scaglietti was involved,

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:14.740
my wife was investigating the incident as a G.A.S. mage.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:20.740
She managed to shut down an illegal research facility and capture some of the test units that had gone out of control.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:27.660
Subaru and Ginga were experimental combat cyborgs that my wife saved while she was following the incident.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:30.620
We couldn’t have kids.

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:36.000
She said that their faces and the color of their hair and eyes were like hers somehow.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:45.600
Anyway, she said that she was going to raise them as our daughters, as humans.

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:51.060
There were some issues with maintenance,
cooperation with research, and the technology involved,

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:53.360
but they were both raised as normal girls.

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:59.510
They were both older when she died.

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:03.450
They said that she died during a secret mission.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:07.410
The truth about the way she died is still classified.

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:15.020
I think she saw something she shouldn’t have and went somewhere she shouldn’t have been.

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:20.300
I’m glad she died the way she wanted, investigating a crime.

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:27.230
But I promised her that I’d raise Ginga and Subaru well.

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:35.470
Well, I kept looking into it. I figured one day I’d have a chance to charge those responsible.

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:43.240
Yagami figured that the combat cyborgs would
get involved with the matter she was dealing with,

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:45.940
and she asked me to help with it.

00:12:45.940 --> 00:12:47.470
That’s one smart little girl!

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:53.700
Well, that’s about all there is to say about my wife and kids.

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:56.320
All that’s left is the joint investigation.

00:12:56.320 --> 00:12:57.040
Ma’am?

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:58.980
Yes, sir.

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:14.980
Combat cyborgs, artificial mages...

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:20.930
Both of them are technologies that
Lt. General Regius tried to develop for the Bureau to use.

00:13:20.930 --> 00:13:22.940
That was a long time ago.

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:27.320
A power that could be mass-produced in a stable environment.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:29.060
If you could avoid having it shut down

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:33.120
for ethical violations and decrease the cost via mass production, it’s actually a very feasible plan.

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:40.270
Was Lt. General Regius continuing that project in secret somewhere?

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:47.530
Scaglietti was the ideal person to entrust that job to.

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:53.450
If he wasn’t an illegal researcher, there’s no doubt he’d go down in history as one of the greatest geniuses of all time.

00:13:53.450 --> 00:14:01.140
I suspect that the Lt. General arranged for Scaglietti to be offered a plea bargain and then waited for the right time.

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:05.890
It’s possible to set up a situation where Scaglietti would mass-produce artificial mages and combat cyborgs,

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:11.120
and Surface HQ would discover this and make it public.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:15.040
If that were the case, upon being discovered,

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.820
it would also be simple enough to incorporate whatever was left into experimental usage.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:19.060
Somewhere in there,

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:23.580
it’s also possible for an investigator who got
too close to discovering the truth to have an accident,

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:26.820
which would also cause several excellent artificial mage samples to be acquired.

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:31.090
I’ll ask you to refrain from telling me any more of your foolish delusions.

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:33.220
I’m merely interested in your opinion.

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:36.420
You’ve been in the Bureau for ten years, right?

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:37.050
That’s right.

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:39.180
The Lt. General has been here forty years.

00:14:39.180 --> 00:14:46.300
And ten years ago, when you were causing
your knights to commit crimes out of fear for your life,

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:50.640
and when that source of the power that has raised you up to a Lieutenant Colonel at your age,

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:58.790
the Book of Darkness, that Lost Logia
that fused with you, was taking many lives,

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:03.460
the Lt. General was working to keep the peace.

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:07.410
I won’t deny the crimes I have committed, nor those of the Book of Darkness,

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:12.920
but if there’s a hidden truth here, I will bring it to light.

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:15.450
That’s my job now.

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:21.880
If you wish to investigate us, then either bring an investigative permit or a warrant.

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:22.900
Then we can talk.

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:25.770
I will, definitely.

00:15:26.850 --> 00:15:30.690
There was a message from the Council earlier.

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:33.660
An emergency hearing will be held
concerning your conduct, Lieutenant General.

00:15:35.110 --> 00:15:37.470
Einherjar’s operations are to be suspended as well.

00:15:38.110 --> 00:15:40.990
It’s an emergency! Continue the operation!

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:42.790
Have the hearing put off!

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:46.250
I’m not going to be his puppet!

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:47.840
I’m the one who was controlling <i>him!</i>

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:51.330
If he’s going to go against us, then I’ll destroy him!

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:54.370
I’ll attend to it immediately.

00:15:55.590 --> 00:15:59.550
Also, there’s something I’d like you to confirm immediately.

00:15:59.550 --> 00:16:00.560
What now?

00:16:01.430 --> 00:16:04.880
This is an image of the U.F.O.
that was heading towards HQ yesterday.

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:09.780
An aerial mage stopped him, but this man...

00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:15.230
Lt. General.

00:16:15.230 --> 00:16:18.110
Lt. General!

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:24.460
Sir!

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:29.400
Sir.

00:16:32.290 --> 00:16:33.870
I’m okay now.

00:16:33.870 --> 00:16:35.120
Sorry

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:36.600
for scaring you.

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:40.050
I’m sorry, sir. It’s my fault for not being useful.

00:16:40.050 --> 00:16:42.540
You did well.

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:48.810
That red knight was a good one,
including her use of her Unight.

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:50.440
You’re stronger than her, sir!

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:54.070
If you’d been at your best, sir,
and if I’d been more useful, she’d be no match!

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:56.520
This is my best now.

00:16:56.520 --> 00:16:58.980
And you did your best as well.

00:16:58.980 --> 00:17:00.040
Hey, Agito?

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:04.990
Can I have another glass of that medicine you made for me?

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:05.700
Yes!

00:17:08.680 --> 00:17:11.210
Knight Zest, it’s Uno.

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:15.670
You seem unwell.

00:17:15.670 --> 00:17:16.920
Don’t worry about me.

00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:21.140
You don’t need me or the Relics anymore, do you?

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:22.880
That’s not true.

00:17:22.880 --> 00:17:25.600
There are a few things I have left to do, that’s all.

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.470
Then I’ll die.

00:17:27.470 --> 00:17:30.870
I don’t think I’ll interfere with your plans.

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:32.810
That’s very sad.

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:36.360
Even if there’s a difference between
you artificial mages and us combat cyborgs,

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:39.330
we should be friends.

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:41.900
I’m different from even you.

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:49.250
I’ve died once, and now I’m just a dead man living for a short time before he returns to dust once again.

00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:55.200
Miss Lutecia finished her examination and tuning earlier.

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:57.430
She should be able to return to you soon.

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:59.030
I see.

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:00.910
Get well soon.

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:04.270
Sir, I brought your medicine.

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:17.530
Yo.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:18.570
Sein.

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:19.910
How’s Cinques?

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:23.870
Her basic frame has been badly damaged, it seems.

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:27.810
That girl—the second 0’s I.S., Oscillating Breaker,

00:18:27.810 --> 00:18:34.870
is extremely effective against the electrical components in our bodies and frames.

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:39.340
Of course, I’m sure it’s pretty strong against normal objects or people as well.

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:43.510
A direct hit from that would be the end of any of us.

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:47.020
Nove, your right arm is going to need a lot of surgery too.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:48.510
I see.

00:18:48.510 --> 00:18:52.940
I’m fine, but Cinques got hit with a bunch of them.

00:18:55.690 --> 00:19:00.610
Our original was born in a different way than us.

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:05.630
There’s no doubt that she’s made from the Doctor’s technology, but we don’t even know who made her.

00:19:05.630 --> 00:19:08.990
I don’t really care about that, and it doesn’t really matter.

00:19:08.990 --> 00:19:14.620
I’m going to <i>demolish</i> that girl with the hair ribbon
who did this to Cinques!

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:17.790
Don’t demolish her! We need to recover her.

00:19:17.790 --> 00:19:20.610
And the ginger illusionist too.

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:23.470
If I hadn’t been so busy dealing with her...

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:25.920
We know, we know.

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:27.890
Let’s get her next time.

00:19:28.840 --> 00:19:31.470
Quattro, the Doctor is calling.

00:19:31.470 --> 00:19:35.940
’Kay! Sein, keep an eye on Cinque, okay?

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:36.860
On it!

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:46.650
Oh, hey Miss Lu!

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:48.890
I’m XI, Wendi!

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:51.810
This is VIII, Otto, and XII, Deed!

00:19:52.660 --> 00:19:56.790
So this is your mom, huh?

00:19:56.790 --> 00:19:57.590
So it seems.

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:58.660
Seems?

00:19:58.660 --> 00:20:01.550
I don’t remember her.

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:12.170
Uh, well... once we find the appropriate Relic core, she’ll come back to life, right?

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:14.400
That’s what the Doctor says.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:18.820
If we find Serial No. XI, she’ll wake up.

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:26.970
And that if she awakens and becomes my mom,
then I’ll finally have a heart.

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:31.780
Hayate.

00:20:31.780 --> 00:20:32.540
Verossa!

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:34.050
I’m sorry to keep you waiting.

00:20:34.050 --> 00:20:37.250
I bet even <i>you</i> are a little down, huh, Hayate?

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:40.030
Well, I guess so.

00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:43.750
It was a major failure,
with Ginga and Vivio getting kidnapped.

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:46.460
Several of my soldiers were hurt.

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:49.800
But we’ll take back what was stolen,

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:52.180
and this time I’ll protect them.

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:55.420
So even if she’s down, she’s still up for the job.

00:20:55.420 --> 00:20:56.900
Pretty nice.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:21:01.860
As Mistress of the Night Sky
and as the head of Riot Force 6, it’s natural.

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:04.980
But are you sure about this?

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:08.280
Since you and Chrono asked for it, Hayate,
I managed to get permission.

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:13.940
We need an HQ so that the staff will have somewhere to live.

00:21:13.940 --> 00:21:17.230
And considering what’s coming, a mobile HQ is better.

00:21:17.230 --> 00:21:23.670
<i>Arthra,</i> we’ll need you to do your best for us for just a little while longer before you go to sleep.

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:28.960
Nanoha?

00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:30.220
Fate.

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:32.580
What are you doing out here?

00:21:33.970 --> 00:21:36.430
Thinking about Vivio?

00:21:36.430 --> 00:21:39.920
Yeah, I couldn’t keep my promise.

00:21:43.770 --> 00:21:48.650
I said I’d be her mother, that I’d protect her.

00:21:48.650 --> 00:21:51.020
But I couldn’t be by her side.

00:21:51.020 --> 00:21:52.740
I couldn’t protect her.

00:21:53.230 --> 00:21:56.210
I’m sure she’s crying now.

00:21:56.990 --> 00:21:58.170
Nanoha.

00:21:58.170 --> 00:22:00.760
When I think about Vivio crying alone,

00:22:00.760 --> 00:22:07.840
and that maybe she’s sad or hurt,
my body shakes, and I feel like I’m about to go crazy.

00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:10.790
I want to go save her right now!

00:22:10.790 --> 00:22:12.760
But I...

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:13.960
It’s okay.

00:22:13.960 --> 00:22:16.710
Vivio is definitely okay.

00:22:19.640 --> 00:22:22.150
Let’s save her together.

00:22:35.660 --> 00:22:37.370
Okay, there we go.

00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:39.080
Don’t be scared.

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:41.030
Vitals are fine.

00:22:41.030 --> 00:22:42.780
Mana output stabilized.

00:22:42.780 --> 00:22:44.570
Transplant preparations complete.

00:22:46.750 --> 00:22:48.470
Perfect timing.

00:22:52.290 --> 00:22:57.540
No! No!

00:23:01.230 --> 00:23:05.020
Mama! Mama!

00:23:09.820 --> 00:23:12.260
Now then, let’s begin.

00:23:12.260 --> 00:23:17.160
We shall now bestow the royal mark
upon the Vessel of the Holy King.

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:23.080
Vivio, you shall be my masterpiece!

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:28.030
Mama!

00:25:17.620 --> 00:25:22.320
With new wings,
Riot Force 6 rises again.

00:25:22.320 --> 00:25:27.010
With resolve in their hearts,
they head for the sky and what appears there.

00:25:33.680 --> 00:25:35.990
Take off!
